      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Self-medicating with any new medication, even a small dose, is risky, especially when interacting with an antidepressant like sertraline. Monitoring yourself alone is not a substitute for professional medical advice when drug interactions are a concern. If your pain is significantly impairing your life, please consider calling your doctor's office again to see if they offer a telehealth consultation. They can advise you on safe, over-the-counter options or the necessity of immediate care.",
      "source": "target",
